// Figure artwork for the strength session — the lifts and nothing else.
//
// Split out of js/stretch-art.js in v58, and the split is about *when* these
// bytes are needed rather than what they are. They are the same kind of data,
// traced the same way (see the header of stretch-art.js, which is still the
// place the pipeline and the "do not round the relative paths" rule are
// written down) — but the lift screen is the only thing that reads them, and
// it is one of nine screens.
//
// So this file is:
//
//   - **imported lazily**, by js/views/strength.js at mount, not by the boot
//     graph. Every other screen used to parse 53 KB of paths it would never
//     draw.
//   - **precached as an EXTRA, not in CORE.** CORE is `cache.addAll`, which is
//     all-or-nothing, and the app has to survive that list failing. A missing
//     figure is not a broken app: `stretchFigure` returns null and the head
//     renders one fewer child, which is the contract PENDING_ART has had since
//     v27. Anything whose absence is silent belongs in the optional half.
//     tests/offline.test.mjs enforces both halves of that rule — a module may
//     only sit outside CORE if it is genuinely imported with `import()`.
//
// The trade, stated plainly: on a phone that has never opened the lift screen
// and then loses signal, the movements draw without figures. That is the same
// deal the voice clips have taken since v53, and it is the right one — the
// alternative is the whole app failing to cache because of a drawing.
//
// `single-leg-rdl` is deliberately NOT here. The lift and the rest-day
// mobility item are the same movement under the same id, so its figure stays
// in stretch-art.js where the routine can reach it without this import.

